详细说明:
The study aims to demonstrate the superiority of a non-invasive strategy based of the analysis of circulating dd-cfDNA (AlloSeq cfDNA assay) to monitor cardiac allograft rejection during the first-year post-transplant compared to the currently recommended invasive biopsy-based strategy.

The primary endpoint will be a hierarchical composite endpoint evaluated at 11-month post-randomization (win-ratio analysis):

1. all-cause mortality or listing for redo heart transplantation;
2. acute allograft dysfunction due to biopsy-proven rejection or other causes (see definition in the detailed protocol);
3. biopsy-related complications (see definition in the detailed protocol);
4. symptoms of anxiety and depression as assessed by the Hospital Anxiety and Depression scale.

The secondary objectives of the study will be:

Safety objectives: analysis of mortality, redo transplantation and usual clinical, histopathologic and echocardiographic parameters of graft function, but also an in-depth allograft evaluation (tissular molecular biology).

Efficiency objectives: The number of biopsies performed in each group will evaluate the potential gain of the non-invasive strategy. This analysis will be completed by a medico-economic analysis to precise the impact of this strategy in the French transplant care environment.

Quality of life of transplant recipients will be assessed using generic and specific scales.

