3. Diagnosed with atherosclerotic cerebrovascular disease;
4. Diagnosed with peripheral artery disease; or without a clinical history of ASCVD, but meeting the definition of high-risk individuals for ASCVD in the overall risk assessment flowchart for ASCVD in Chinese lipid management guidelines (2023) (see Appendix 16.1 for the overall risk assessment flowchart for ASCVD in Chinese adults);
6. For the trial participants who receive the following drug treatments, their treatment plans must be stable for at least 4 weeks before signing the screening ICF, and are expected to remain stable until the end of the follow-up period after the last administration of the trial drug:

1. Lipid-lowering drugs (statins, ezetimibe, PCSK9 inhibitors, niacin, fibrates, fish oil or other products containing ω-3 fatty acids, including over-the-counter drugs \[OTC\]);
2. Testosterone, estrogen, anti-estrogen, progesterone, progestin, selective estrogen receptor modulators and growth hormone.
7. Female trial participants are not pregnant or breastfeeding; fertile female and male trial participants must have an acceptable contraceptive method from the time of signing the ICF until 12 months after the last administration of the trial drug (see Appendix 16.2 for the requirements for trial participants' contraception); males are not allowed to donate sperm, and females are not allowed to donate eggs;
8. They are willing to follow the research procedures stipulated in this protocol (including follow-up) and are willing to cooperate fully with the researchers.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Clinical evidence of active liver disease or liver dysfunction in the past or currently exists, defined as AST or ALT ≥ 2 times the upper limit of normal (ULN) or total bilirubin (TBIL) ≥ 1.5 times the ULN at the screening period (except for participants diagnosed with Gilbert syndrome);
2. Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) calculated using the Chronic Kidney Disease - Epidemiology Collaboration (CKD-EPI) creatinine clearance formula is \ 14 days is considered stable use); or regular systemic corticosteroid use within 4 weeks before the first dose; or expected need for prednisone \>20 mg/day or equivalent;
18. Currently receiving, or having received lipoprotein apheresis within 3 months before randomization, or planning to receive lipoprotein apheresis during the study;
19. Have homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia (HoFH) or have received lomitapide within 12 months prior to randomization;
20. Are known to be allergic to any component of YKYY032 injection, or have a history or current severe allergic reaction;
21. Have participated in or plan to participate in a drug clinical trial within 3 months prior to screening, or within the trial period (excluding non-interventional studies and those who only signed the ICF but did not receive study intervention);
22. Have had or currently have drug abuse or alcoholism (for men, an average weekly alcohol intake of more than 14 units, for women, more than 7 units \[1 unit = 360 mL beer; or 150 mL wine; or 45 mL distilled spirits\]);
23. Have received any known herbal medicine (including but not limited to: hawthorn, salvia miltiorrhiza), vitamin (including but not limited to: niacin), or supplement (including but not limited to: red yeast rice, omega-3 fatty acids) within 30 days prior to randomization, except for those who have been using lipid-lowering drugs stably for 4 weeks prior to screening (see item 6 of the inclusion criteria);
24. Have had or currently have any underlying disease or mental condition that the investigator considers may affect the safety of the study participants during the study, or interfere with the participation or completion of the study, or affect the interpretation of data.

