6. clinically stable as indicated by no antipsychotic medication changes in the last month or if on depot, no change in the past 2 months.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. history of intellectual disability, or developmental or neurological disorder;
2. history of brain trauma associated with loss of consciousness for \> 10 minutes or behavioral sequelae;
3. alcohol or substance use disorder within the last 6 months; and
4. history of eye disease (e.g., glaucoma, retinopathy).

Inclusion Criteria:

1. Men and women aged 50 to 86 years;
2. Able to fully comprehend and sign an informed consent form;
3. Fulfill diagnostic criteria for Mild Cognitive Impairment (MCI), as outlined by Albert and colleagues, and indicated by: 1. concern about a change in cognition, in comparison with the person's previous level, expressed by the participant, an informant who knows the patient well, or an investigator; 2. Montreal Cognitive Assessment (MoCA) score lower than or equal to 26; 3. general preservation of independence in functional abilities; 4. no dementia.
4. Fulfill the diagnostic criteria for PSCI/subcortical vascular cognitive impairment that developed after the documented stroke/TIA, as outlined by Skrobot and colleagues. This requires the presence of a cognitive syndrome (as defined in Section A below) and SVD (as defined in Section B below). Impairment in at least one cognitive domain and mild to no impairment in instrumental activities of daily living (IADLs)/activities of daily living (ADLs), respectively (independent of the motor/ sensory sequelae of the vascular event); A. Cognitive Syndrome defined as: 1. Dysexecutive Syndrome: Some impairment in goal formulation, initiation, planning, organizing, sequencing, executing, set-shifting and maintenance, or abstracting; 2. Memory Deficit: Some impairment in recall, relative intact recognition, less severe forgetting, benefit from cues. B. Small Vessel Ischaemic Disease defined as: Evidence of relevant cerebrovascular disease by brain imaging (in the last 1-24 months) defined as the presence of both: (i) Periventricular and deep WMLs (grading scale \>1 on the Fazekas score) plus at least one lacunar infarct; and (ii) Absence of cortical and/or cortico-sub-cortical non-lacunar territorial infarcts and watershed infarcts, indicating large vessel disease, signs of normal pressure hydrocephalus, or other specific causes of WML.
5. Presence or a history of neurological signs as evidence for cerebrovascular disease at least 1 month prior to enrollment.
6. Community-dwelling;
7. Able to comply with scheduled visits, treatment plan, and other trial procedures;
8. Able to walk independently;
9. Modified Rankin score \<2.
10. Willing to have a study partner (see Appendix 1 for definition of study partner) throughout the study.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Patients diagnosed with dementia or significant cognitive impairment as defined by a MoCA score \<17 at screening and clinical evaluation excluding diagnosis of dementia, or other neurological conditions (multiple sclerosis, Parkinson's disease, epilepsy, etc.) that affects cognition and mobility;
2. Hemorrhages and cerebral edema (e.g., subarachnoid hemorrhage, intracerebral hemorrhage, subdural hematoma, epidural hematoma).
3. Patients in a state of coma or with severe disturbance of consciousness, aphasia, agnosia, or deafness that subsequently affects expression and communication.
4. Significant acute medical illness including: drug overdose, severely disturbed liver, kidney or lung function, anemia, hypothyroidism, or uncontrolled diabetes
5. Presence of cortical involvement on neurologic examination including aphasia, extinsion etc.;
6. Diagnosed previously with a genetic cause of VCI (e.g., CADASIL);
7. Taking medications that may negatively affect cognitive function;
8. Unable to meet the specific scanning requirements of the 3T MRI;
9. History of hepatitis or elevated hepatic transaminases or bilirubin; positive serology for Hepatitis B or C; positive serology for HIV;
10. Serum creatinine over 1.8;
11. Subject has a current or past diagnosis of bipolar or related disorders, intellectual disability, or cluster b personality disorder (e.g., borderline personality disorder, antisocial personality disorder, histrionic personality disorder, and narcissistic personality disorder), psychotic disorder, schizophrenia, obsessive-compulsive disorder, and substance/alcohol use disorders other than nicotine in the past year (including barbiturates, methadone, opiates, cocaine, cannabinoids, and amphetamine/ methamphetamine).
12. Subject has suicidal ideation with intent to act during screening phase or on Day 1, or has a history of suicidal behavior within the past year.
13. Diagnosis of attention deficit disorder;
14. Prolongation of the corrected QT (CTc) interval;
15. Use of drugs with possible interactions with Maraviroc.
16. Subject has known allergies, hypersensitivity, intolerance, or contraindication to Maraviroc or its excipients.
17. Subject has received an investigational drug (including investigational vaccines) or used an invasive investigational medical device within 60 days before the planned first dose of study drug or is currently enrolled in an investigational study.
18. Subject has any condition for which, in the opinion of the investigator, participation would not be in the best interest of the subject (e.g., compromise the well-being) or that could prevent, limit, or confound the protocol-specified assessments.
19. Subject has had major surgery, (e.g., requiring general anesthesia) within 2 weeks before screening, or will not have fully recovered from surgery, or has surgery planned during the time the subject is expected to participate in the study.
20. Subject is a woman who is pregnant, breast-feeding, or planning to become pregnant while enrolled in this study or within 3 months after the last dose of study drug.

简要说明:
The goal of this observational study is to learn about the pathophysiological characterization and evolutionary patterns of Alzheimer's disease (AD) in older adults in Fujian Province, China. The primary purposes are as follows:

1. establishment and follow-up of cohorts in the general population and populations with cognitive impairment;
2. investigation of risk factors and evolutionary patterns of AD pathological characteristics;
3. construction and validation of AD digital phenotypes based on multi-dimensional digital-intelligence screening;
4. exploration of AD-related risk genes and their mechanisms of action;
5. development of novel technologies for plasma biomarkers and PET imaging for the accurate diagnosis of AD.

入组条件:
Inclusion Criteria:

1. Age between 55 and 90 years, both sexes eligible;
2. Educational level of primary school or above, or with a sound working history, excluding individuals with intellectual disability;
3. Able to speak Mandarin fluently and capable of completing the full battery of neuropsychological assessments;
4. Geriatric Depression Scale (GDS) score ≤ 6;
5. Adequate visual and auditory function to complete all neuropsychological tests successfully;
6. Willing and able to provide peripheral blood samples and to undergo brain PET and MRI neuroimaging examinations;
7. If taking relevant medications, the dosage must have been stable for at least 4 weeks. Specific medication requirements: stable doses of antidepressants are permitted, provided that the participant has no significant anticholinergic adverse effects and no history of major depressive episode within the past year; estrogen replacement therapy is allowed; Ginkgo biloba preparations may be taken, but routine use is not recommended; use of any psychoactive drugs is prohibited within 4 weeks prior to screening.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Coexisting severe neurological disorders, including Parkinson's disease, multi-infarct dementia, Huntington's disease, normal pressure hydrocephalus, intracranial tumors, progressive supranuclear palsy, epilepsy, subdural hematoma, multiple sclerosis, etc.; history of severe traumatic brain injury with persistent neurological deficits, or history of definite structural brain abnormalities;
2. Brain MRI findings indicating intracranial infection, cerebral infarction, focal organic lesions, or multiple lacunar infarcts in key memory-related brain regions;
3. Contraindications to MRI, such as implanted cardiac pacemakers, or the presence of metallic foreign bodies or fragments within the body;
4. Diagnosis of major depressive disorder or bipolar disorder according to DSM-5 criteria within the past 1 year; presence of psychotic symptoms, agitation, or aggressive behavior within the past 3 months that would preclude compliance with the study protocol;
5. Past history of schizophrenia, or current pharmacotherapy for obsessive-compulsive disorder or attention deficit disorder;
6. History of alcohol or substance abuse or dependence meeting DSM-5 criteria within the past 2 years;
7. Concomitant severe systemic diseases or unstable general medical conditions that would preclude participation in the longitudinal follow-up of this study;
8. Clinically significant abnormalities in serum vitamin B12 or thyroid function indicators, with direct exclusion for those presenting with decreased vitamin B12 levels;
9. Current use of psychoactive drugs, including antidepressants, neuroleptics, long-acting anxiolytics, or sedative-hypnotics; long-term use of anticoagulants such as warfarin, dabigatran, rivaroxaban, or apixaban (except for lumbar puncture procedures);
10. Concurrent participation in other neuropsychiatric clinical studies.

